      "id": 1,
      "text": "Lisbon Falls was incorporated as Thompsonborough in 1799 and renamed Lisbon in 1802 after Portugal’s capital.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://winslowmaine.org/lisbon-maine-exploring-the-hidden-gems-of-the-pine-tree-state"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Historic textile mills along the Androscoggin River, especially the Worumbo Mill founded in 1864, shaped Lisbon Falls’ industrial heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://winslowmaine.org/lisbon-maine-exploring-the-hidden-gems-of-the-pine-tree-state"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Worumbo Mill, the town’s main mill, burned down in 1987, ending a century of wool production.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://winslowmaine.org/lisbon-maine-exploring-the-hidden-gems-of-the-pine-tree-state"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Papermill Trail offers a 1.7‑mile, wheelchair‑accessible walk along the Androscoggin and Sabattus rivers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
